{"path":"iterator/indirectly_copyable_storable","title":"std::indirectly_copyable_storable","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>indirectly_copyable_storable","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/iterator/indirectly_copyable_storable","section":"iterator","kind":"page","summary":"The indirectly_copyable_storable concept specifies the relationship between an indirectly_readable type and an indirectly_writable type.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/iterator\">&lt;iterator&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> In, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> Out <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>concept indirectly_copyable_storable <span class=\"sy1\">=</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/indirectly_copyable\"><span class=\"kw3143\">std::<span class=\"me2\">indirectly_copyable</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>In, Out<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/indirectly_writable\"><span class=\"kw2876\">std::<span class=\"me2\">indirectly_writable</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Out, <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/iter_t\"><span class=\"kw2890\">std::<span class=\"me2\">iter_value_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>In<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/indirectly_writable\"><span class=\"kw2876\">std::<span class=\"me2\">indirectly_writable</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Out, <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/iter_t\"><span class=\"kw2890\">std::<span class=\"me2\">iter_value_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>In<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/indirectly_writable\"><span class=\"kw2876\">std::<span class=\"me2\">indirectly_writable</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Out, <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/iter_t\"><span class=\"kw2890\">std::<span class=\"me2\">iter_value_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>In<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/indirectly_writable\"><span class=\"kw2876\">std::<span class=\"me2\">indirectly_writable</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Out, <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/iter_t\"><span class=\"kw2890\">std::<span class=\"me2\">iter_value_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>In<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/concepts/copyable\"><span class=\"kw2973\">std::<span class=\"me2\">copyable</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/iter_t\"><span class=\"kw2890\">std::<span class=\"me2\">iter_value_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>In<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/concepts/constructible_from\"><span class=\"kw2964\">std::<span class=\"me2\">constructible_from</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/iter_t\"><span class=\"kw2890\">std::<span class=\"me2\">iter_value_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>In<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/iter_t\"><span class=\"kw2891\">std::<span class=\"me2\">iter_reference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>In<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/concepts/assignable_from\"><span class=\"kw2960\">std::<span class=\"me2\">assignable_from</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/iter_t\"><span class=\"kw2890\">std::<span class=\"me2\">iter_value_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>In<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/iter_t\"><span class=\"kw2891\">std::<span class=\"me2\">iter_reference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>In<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The <code>indirectly_copyable_storable</code> concept specifies the relationship between an <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/indirectly_readable\"><code>indirectly_readable</code></a> type and an <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/indirectly_writable\"><code>indirectly_writable</code></a> type. In addition to <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/indirectly_copyable\"><code>indirectly_copyable</code></a>, this concept specifies that the copy from the <code>indirectly_readable</code> type can be performed via an intermediate object.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Semantic_requirements\">Semantic requirements</h3>\n<p><code>In</code> and <code>Out</code> model <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">indirectly_copyable_storable</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>In, Out<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code> only if given a dereferenceable value <code>i</code> of type <code>In</code>:\n</p>\n<ul><li> After the definition <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/iter_t\"><span class=\"kw2890\">std::<span class=\"me2\">iter_value_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>In<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> obj<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>i<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code>, <code>obj</code> is equal to the value previously denoted by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>i</span></code>, and\n</li><li> if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/iter_t\"><span class=\"kw2891\">std::<span class=\"me2\">iter_reference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>In<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code> is an rvalue reference type, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>i</span></code> is placed in a valid but unspecified state after the initialization of <code>obj</code>.\n</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"Equality_preservation\">Equality preservation</h3>\n<p>Expressions declared in <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/requires\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">requires</span> expressions</a> of the standard library concepts are required to be <a href=\"/w/cpp/concepts#Equality_preservation\">equality-preserving</a> (except where stated otherwise).\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/indirectly_copyable\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>indirectly_copyable</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  specifies that values may be copied from an <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/indirectly_readable\"><code>indirectly_readable</code></a> type to an <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/indirectly_writable\"><code>indirectly_writable</code></a> type <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(concept)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/indirectly_movable_storable\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>indirectly_movable_storable</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  specifies that values may be moved from an <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/indirectly_readable\"><code>indirectly_readable</code></a> type to an <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/indirectly_writable\"><code>indirectly_writable</code></a> type and that the move may be performed via an intermediate object <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(concept)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Semantic requirements","id":"Semantic_requirements"},{"depth":3,"text":"Equality preservation","id":"Equality_preservation"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"iterator","title":"Iterator library"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::indirectly_copyable_storable","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++20. The indirectly_copyable_storable concept specifies the relationship between an indirectly_readable type and an…"},{"label":"Semantic requirements","note":"In and Out model std::indirectly_copyable_storable<In, Out> only if given a dereferenceable value i of type In:"},{"label":"Equality preservation","note":"Expressions declared in requires expressions of the standard library concepts are required to be equality-preserving (except where stated otherwise)."},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"indirectly_copyable","note":"specifies that values may be copied from an indirectly_readable type to an indirectly_writable type"},{"label":"indirectly_movable_storable","note":"specifies that values may be moved from an indirectly_readable type to an indirectly_writable type and that the move may be performed via an intermediate object"}]}]},"standards":["C++20"],"wordCount":194,"codeBlockCount":0}
